  "notes": "FILED ON THE MAGNITUDE TRIGGER ONLY (delta -8.7). NO BAND CHANGE — Developing sustained at both the published 40.0 and the assessed 31.3, so the band-crossing evidence test is not applicable. RECOMMENDATION IS flag-for-review AND THE SCORE IS NOT THE POINT. THE DOMINANT FINDING IS AN ENTITY-RECORD DEFECT: Interpublic Group was acquired by Omnicom Group and the merger completed in November 2025. IPG no longer exists as an independent Fortune-500 company, and its standalone index entry at rank 179 is stale. This is the same defect class as the \"Automatic Data Process\" duplicate merged into \"ADP\" on 2026-08-17. The correct remedy is an entity-record decision (merge into an Omnicom entry, retire, or retain with annotation), NOT a score change; applying a score to a company that no longer independently exists would be misleading at any value. ATTRIBUTION: the 3,200 roles IPG cut globally in 2025 are IPG own-conduct while independent and are scored. The further 4,000-plus post-merger layoffs and agency-brand retirements were announced by OMNICOM and are NOT scored against IPG. CONFIDENCE IS LOW: no compassion-relevant evidence was found in the 14-day scan window and the corporate status is unresolved. DO NOT APPLY A SCORE UNTIL THE ENTITY RECORD IS RESOLVED.",
